# component: empty
# decisions: API-16, API-22, API-29, DOC-2, TYP-15
# hunks:
#   API-29: `Empty` takes `size="sm"` (`data-size`), the compact inline empty: a 16px padding, an
#     8px gap and no media margin.
#   API-29: `Empty` always renders an icon — an `icon` prop, lucide `Inbox` by default — as a
#     leading `EmptyMedia variant="icon"` marked `data-default`, hidden by a `:has()` rule when the
#     composition brings its own `EmptyMedia`. `React` types and the lucide import come with it.
#   TYP-15: the title's `tracking-tight` is dropped. TYP-15 puts the heading tier's optical
#     tracking in the theme and holds the COPY tier at zero, which is Geist's own copy/heading
#     split; this title is `text-sm` (14px), squarely in the copy tier, where negative tracking
#     costs legibility and buys nothing. It was the only copy-tier tracking in the registry.
#   API-22: `EmptyTitle` renders through Base UI's `useRender` (upstream's own Badge pattern:
#     `mergeProps` + `render` + `state.slot`) instead of a fixed `<div>`, so a page sets the heading
#     level on the part (`render={<h2 />}`). The default tag, the `data-slot` and the class list are
#     upstream's, unchanged.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is added — `useRender` calls `React.useRef` internally, so the module
#     throws on import in an RSC without the boundary (`verify-rsc-safety.mjs`).
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file; those hunks carry no decision of their own.
